<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The logo as the splash screen should draw it: inside the circular safe zone, so nothing clips it.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
  `ic_launcher_foreground` is a rounded square that fills its whole canvas — which is right for the
  launcher, where the system mask is a squircle on most devices and the mark reads edge to edge (the
  dock shows exactly that). The splash is not the launcher: it draws the icon inside a CIRCLE, so the
  four corners of a full-bleed square are cut off and the brand mark arrives on screen as a disc.
  Measured on the Galaxy S9 before this change.

  The fix is geometry, not a new asset. A square inscribed in a circle has a side of 1/sqrt(2) of the
  diameter, i.e. about 71 % — so an inset of ~15 % per side is the mathematical minimum. 16 % is used
  here for a margin, and because it is the value the rest of the portfolio already uses for the same
  reason (Notes Tech insets its adaptive foreground by 16 %).

  Deliberately NOT applied to `mipmap/ic_launcher`: the launcher mask is a squircle, the full-bleed
  mark fits it, and insetting there would shrink the icon on the home screen for no reason. One asset,
  two framings, each sized for the shape that will actually clip it.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground"
    android:inset="16%" />
